<!--
  sui-markdown.before.sui — EXISTING look (repo). Renders model/doc markdown as
  prose. Minimal styling: bold headings, default browser spacing, a muted code
  chip, hairline table. Representative content inlined (design mock). Compiled as
  <x-markdown-before>.
-->
<style>
  :host { display: block; font-family: var(--font-body); color: var(--foreground); font-size: var(--text-md); }
  .md { line-height: 1.5; }
  .md h2 { font-size: var(--text-xl); font-weight: 700; }
  .md h3 { font-size: var(--text-lg); font-weight: 700; }
  .md code { font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: var(--text-sm); background: var(--muted); padding: 1px 4px; border-radius: var(--radius-sm); }
  .md a { color: var(--primary); }
  .md blockquote { margin: var(--space-3) 0; padding-left: var(--space-3); color: var(--muted-foreground); border-left: 3px solid var(--border); }
  .md table { border-collapse: collapse; font-size: var(--text-sm); }
  .md th, .md td { border: 1px solid var(--border); padding: 4px 8px; text-align: left; }
</style>
<div class="md" part="prose">
  <h2>Reindex runbook</h2>
  <p>Run a <strong>dry-run</strong> first. The reindex is idempotent per shard, so it's safe to retry. See <a href="#">the design doc</a> for the rollback path.</p>
  <h3>Steps</h3>
  <ol>
    <li>Pause the write queue.</li>
    <li>Trigger <code>ship reindex --dry-run</code>.</li>
    <li>Confirm the diff, then drop <code>--dry-run</code>.</li>
  </ol>
  <blockquote>Heads up: holding the queue past 5 minutes pages the on-call.</blockquote>
  <h3>Budgets</h3>
  <table>
    <thead><tr><th>Metric</th><th>Target</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td>p99 latency</td><td>240 ms</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Error rate</td><td>0.1%</td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>
</div>
